      "id": "DCJ-01",
      "chapter": "global",
      "anchor": "global-deep-chart-jacobian",
      "title": "Riemannian Haar gauge and the ordered exponential-cube Jacobian bound",
      "hypotheses": "An integer dimension n ≥ 0, a sign vector ε ∈ {±1}ⁿ defining J_ε = diag(ε₁, …, ε_n), the real unitary group U(ε) = {u ∈ GL_n(ℂ) : u* J_ε u = J_ε} with real Lie algebra 𝔤_ε = {X ∈ M_n(ℂ) : X* J_ε + J_ε X = 0} of real dimension n² equipped with Re tr(X Y*) and Hilbert–Schmidt norm ‖·‖_HS, a left Haar measure μ_ε on U(ε), a real orthonormal basis E₁, …, E_{n²} ∈ 𝔤_ε defining Θ(t) = exp(t₁ E₁) ⋯ exp(t_{n²} E_{n²}), and a cube side length s > 0 satisfying n(exp(3n²s) − 1) ≤ 1/2.",
      "statement": "There exists a unique positive scalar c_ε > 0 such that c_ε μ_ε({u ∈ U(ε) : ‖u − 1‖_HS ≤ r}) / r^(n²) → ω_{n²} as r → 0⁺, where ω_{n²} is the Lebesgue volume of the unit Euclidean ball in ℝ^(n²); and for every nonnegative measurable function Φ : U(ε) → [0, ∞], ∫_{[0,s]^(n²)} Φ(Θ(t)) dt ≤ exp(2n³(exp(2n²s) − 1)) · c_ε ∫_{Θ([0,s]^(n²))} Φ(y) dμ_ε(y). When 8n⁵s ≤ 1 and 12n³s ≤ 1, the exponential prefactor is at most e at each of the f real places.",
      "definitions": [
        "Riemannian Haar gauge constant c_ε > 0 calibrated against unit Euclidean ball volume ω_{n²} in Hilbert–Schmidt metric",
        "ordered product exponential chart Θ(t) = exp(t₁ E₁) ⋯ exp(t_{n²} E_{n²}) on ℝ^(n²)",
        "operator-norm derivative distortion bound δ = n(exp(2n²s) − 1) ≤ 1/2"
      ],
      "equations": [
        "global-deep-haar-gauge-eq",
        "global-deep-ordered-chart-eq"
      ],
